**Given:**

1 + sqrt{ {cotθ + cosθ} over cotθ - cosθ} 

0° θ 

**Formula used:**

1 - sin² θ = cos² θ

**Calculation:**

1 + sqrt{ {cotθ + cosθ} over cotθ - cosθ} 

⇒ 1+sqrt{(frac{cos θ)/(sin θ)+cos θ}{(cos θ)/(sin θ)-cos θ}} 

⇒ 1+sqrt{(frac{cos θ)/(sin θtimes cos θ)+1}{(cos θ)/(sin θtimes cos θ)-1}} = 1+sqrt{(frac{1)/(sin θ)+1}{(1)/(sin θ)-1}} 

⇒ 1+sqrt{(frac{1+sin θ)/(sin θ)}{(1-sin θ)/(sin θ)}} = 1 + sqrt{(1+sin θ)/(1-sin θ)}

⇒ 1+sqrt{(1+sin θ)/(1-sin θ)times(1+sin θ)/(1+sin θ)} 

⇒ 1+sqrt{((1+sin θ)²)/(1-sin² θ)} = 1+sqrt{((1+sin θ)²)/(cos² θ)} 

⇒ 1 + {1+ sintheta}over{costheta}

⇒ 1 + 1over costheta + sinthetaover costheta

⇒ 1 + sec θ + tan θ

**∴ The value of the given expression is 1 + sec θ + tan θ**

